# Accepted Trivy findings for the API image. One CVE per line, each with a reason.
# `exp:` makes the entry lapse so it is re-reviewed (e.g. once Ubuntu ships a fix).

# glibc fopen heap overflow: needs an attacker-controlled fopen mode string; .NET never
# passes one. Unfixed in Ubuntu 24.04 libc6.
CVE-2026-18374 exp:2027-01-31

# glibc nscd stack overflow: the chiseled image ships no nscd daemon. Unfixed in Ubuntu 24.04 libc6.
CVE-2026-89092 exp:2027-01-31

# ICU SRBRoot::addTag stack overflow: reached only when compiling resource bundles (genrb),
# never by ICU's runtime APIs the app uses. Unfixed in Ubuntu 24.04 libicu74.
CVE-2025-5222 exp:2027-01-31
